// CUE — Timer Warning v2 (4 beeps + 1 higher; NO landing note)
// Status: DONE (owner-approved 2026-08-10, polish session — REPLACES the 2026-07-19
//   escalating six-note ladder, which the owner disliked at both timer endings)
// Plays: last 5 seconds of the DRAWING and JUDGING timers (same cue for both). ONE-SHOT — never loops.
// Design (owner): four identical soft beeps, then a fifth one step higher that IS the landing —
//   it must hit the end of the timer precisely (owner, 2026-08-10 post-render). No ding after it
//   (the owner cut the ding); the next phase's own audio (M6 / S4 / S1) carries what follows.
// Notes: F4 ×4 then A4, triangle (the UI voice) | Tempo: setcpm(60), 1 cycle = 1 s
// Wiring spec: the A4 is the landing note — CUE_LANDING_SEC = 4.046 s (measured onset in the
//   render, ~46 ms engine attack latency included); start playback at T-minus-4.046 s so the A4
//   lands ON the phase-change frame, four F4 beeps counting down before it. The trailing ~0.95 s
//   of file silence plays out harmlessly. The music-fade-into-the-cue behavior (drawing) stays.
// Render: one-shot WAV, cycles 0–5 (~5 s + short tail).
// Paste into https://strudel.cc — inventory: TDD/sound-design-brief.md §3, identity rules §0

setcpm(60)
// One cycle = 1 second. Five cycles = the last five seconds. Play once, do NOT loop.

note("<f4 f4 f4 f4 a4>")
  .sound("triangle")
  .attack(.002).decay(.2).sustain(0).release(.06)
  .lpf(2200)
  .gain("<.42 .42 .42 .42 .5>")
  .room(.15).size(2)
